"]},{"seq":122,"type":"text","at":"2026-07-26T19:40:40.948222328Z","text":"Good progress! Three fixable errors:\n\n1. `totallyBounded_subtype` — wrong name. Let me find the correct one.\n2. `|f x - 0| ≤ r` should be `|f x| ≤ r` — need `sub_zero` not `zero_sub`.\n3. `(lt_div_iff₀ hN_pos).mpr hquot` — `lt_div_iff₀ : a < b/c ↔ a*c < b`, so `.mpr` expects `N * |x-y| < |f x - f y|`. But `hquot : N < |f x - f y| / |x - y|`. The rewrite goes the wrong way — I should use `.mp` or rewrite the other direction. Actually: from `hquot : N < |f x - f y| / |x - y|`, apply `(lt_div_iff₀ hxy_pos).mp hquot` gives `N * |x - y| < |f x - f y|`."},{"seq":123,"type":"tool_use","at":"2026-07-26T19:40:40.970885176Z","tools":["run_shell"],"previews":["run_shell cd /home/joe/code/apm-lean && grep -rn \"totallyBounded.*subtype\\|TotallyBounded.*Subtype\\|Subtype.*totallyBounded\\|total"]},{"seq":124,"type":"text","at":"2026-07-26T19:40:41.513439457Z","text":"[auto-continue 3/8]"},{"seq":125,"type":"tool_use","at":"2026-07-26T19:40:45.781157724Z","tools":["run_shell"],"previews":["run_shell cd /home/joe/code/apm-lean && grep -rn \"TotallyBounded.*subtype\\|totallyBounded.*Subtype\\|subtype.*totallyBounded\\|total"]},{"seq":126,"type":"text","at":"2026-07-26T19:41:02.135372544Z","text":"There's no `totallyBounded_subtype` lemma directly. Let me try a completely different approach for the boundedness proof. Instead of going through subtypes, I can use the direct metric approach: `(0,1)` is bounded (totally bounded), and `UniformContinuousOn` preserves total boundedness on the image. But the cleanest way in Mathlib might be through `IsClosedEmbedding` or `Set.image`.\n\nActually, let me try using `TotallyBounded.image` with `(Subtype.val : I01 → ℝ)` composed with `f`. Since `Subtype.val` is uniformly continuous, and `f ∘ Subtype.val` is the restriction. But `f` is only `UniformContinuousOn`, not global. The restriction to the subtype IS uniformly continuous.\n\nLet me try yet another approach: bypass the totally bounded machinery entirely and use `Metric.isBounded_iff` directly:"},{"seq":127,"type":"tool_use","at":"2026-07-26T19:41:02.139285599Z","tools":["edit_file"],"previews":["edit_file /home/joe/code/apm-lean/problems/a93A01/lean/Main.lean"]},{"seq":128,"type":"text","at":"2026-07-26T19:41:07.092055393Z","text":"The chaining approach is getting very messy. ✘ I should go back to the totally bounded approach but find the right Mathlib API. Let me try `TotallyBounded.image` directly with the subtype, or find a `UniformContinuousOn` version of bounded image. Let me search more carefully:"},{"seq":129,"type":"tool_use","at":"2026-07-26T19:41:07.115636708Z","tools":["run_shell"],"previews":["run_shell cd /home/joe/code/apm-lean && grep -rn \"TotallyBounded.*range\\|TotallyBounded.*image\\|totallyBounded.*range\" .lake/packa"]},{"seq":130,"type":"text","at":"2026-07-26T19:41:16.328458054Z","text":"`TotallyBounded.image` at line 663: `TotallyBounded s → UniformContinuous f → TotallyBounded (f '' s)`. The key issue is that it needs `UniformContinuous` (global on `α`), while I have `UniformContinuousOn f I01`.\n\nLet me look at this differently. If I define `g : I01 → ℝ` by `g = I01.restrict f`, then `g` is `UniformContinuous` (from `h_uc.restrict`). And `Set.univ : Set I01` is totally bounded if `I01` is totally bounded. The question is how to get `TotallyBounded (Set.univ : Set I01)`.\n\n`TotallyBounded` on the subtype `I01` means: `TotallyBounded (Set.univ : Set I01)`. This should follow from `TotallyBounded I01` via the uniform isomorphism between the subtype and the set."},{"seq":131,"type":"tool_use","at":"2026-07-26T19:41:16.341121355Z","tools":["run_shell"],"previews":["run_shell cd /home/joe/code/apm-lean && grep -rn \"totallyBounded.*univ\\|TotallyBounded.*univ\\|totallyBounded_univ\" .lake/packages/"]},{"seq":132,"type":"text","at":"2026-07-26T19:41:24.374310332Z","text":"`Subtype.val` is uniformly continuous. But I need total boundedness of `Set.univ : Set I01`, i.e., of the entire subtype space. This follows from the total boundedness of the underlying set `I01` and the fact that the subtype is uniformly isomorphic to the set.\n\nActually, let me try using `TotallyBounded.subtype_image` or proving it directly:\n\nLet me try the simplest possible approach: skip the totally bounded machinery and prove boundedness using the sequential/ε-δ definition directly, but with a cleaner argument. The key insight: for any `x ∈ (0,1)`, connect `x` to `1/2` via the line segment. Cover `[min(x,1/2), max(x,1/2)]` with finitely many intervals of radius `δ/2`. By UC, `|f| varies by at most 1 per step. With at most `⌈1/δ⌉ + 1` steps, `|f(x)| ≤ |f(1/2)| + ⌈1/δ⌉ + 1`.\n\nBut formalizing this requires `Finset.Icc` or similar partitioning. Let me use `Nat.ceil` and a simpler bound:\n\nFor any `x ∈ (0,1)`: `|x - 1/2| < 1/2`. Cover with `n = max 1 ⌈1/(2δ)⌉` intervals. Then `|f(x) - f(1/2)| ≤ n` (each step ≤ 1 by UC with ε=1). So `|f(x)| ≤ |f(1/2)| + n`.\n\nBut the partition argument is hard in Lean. Let me instead use `Metric.isBounded_iff_ediam_ne_top` and `ediam_image_le_of_uniformContinuousOn` or something. \n\nActually, the cleanest path might be: prove the lemma `TotallyBounded (Set.univ : Set I01)` directly using `totallyBounded_iff`:"},{"seq":133,"type":"tool_use","at":"2026-07-26T19:41:24.392236850Z","tools":["run_shell"],"previews":["run_shell cd /home/joe/code/apm-lean && grep -B2 -A6 \"theorem TotallyBounded.image\" .lake/packages/mathlib/Mathlib/Topology/Unifor"]},{"seq":134,"type":"text","at":"2026-07-26T19:41:32.183135302Z","text":"OK so `TotallyBounded.image` needs `f : α → β` and `UniformContinuous f`. The restriction `I01.restrict f : I01 → ℝ` is uniformly continuous. And `Set.univ : Set I01` — is it totally bounded?\n\n`Set.univ : Set α` is totally bounded iff `α` is totally bounded as a uniform space. For a subtype `{x : α // p x}`, this is totally bounded iff `{x : α // p x}` (the subtype) is totally bounded. And the